# No Three-Dots on Accordion Headers

The accordion section headers on All Modules (`pages/all-modules.html` /
`js/all-modules-flow.js`) must **never** show a ⋮ / ⋯.

This is a permanent, non-negotiable rule. The user has asked for these gone
more than once. Do not put them back.

## What is banned

- `moduleControlsHTML(...)` rendering a `.panel-more-btn` / `more_vert` on
  `.mi-module-head`
- A sticky-modules fallback ⋯ on an accordion header
- Any other kebab, more-options control, or “module options” cluster on the
  accordion label row

`moduleControlsHTML` returns an empty string on purpose. Do not restore the
old markup.

## What still stays

- Ready pills (WIP Ready / AI Ready) on the header
- The expand chevron
- ⋮ menus **inside** an opened section (catalog specimens, table row menus,
  the chat demo) — those are not accordion labels
- The page-level module ⋯ on `#agent-main` itself

## Rules for the agent

- Never add a three-dot to `.mi-module-head`.
- If you touch an accordion header, confirm it has no `.panel-more-btn`.
- If a ⋮ reappears on those rows, remove it — do not restyle it.
